---
import "./infoSection.css";
---

<section class="content-container" id="index-main-content">
  <div class="content" id="summary">
    <h1>WHO WE ARE</h1>
    <p>
      Sidus Robotics is Memorial University's first-ever Mars rover design team,
      comprised of a diverse group of students from engineering, computer
      science, and business. We are preparing to compete in the 2026 Canadian
      International Rover Challenge (CIRC), where university teams design and
      build a rover capable of operating in Mars-like conditions. By taking on
      this challenge, Sidus Robotics not only provides members with invaluable
      real-world experience but also puts Newfoundland and Memorial University
      on the national stage in space robotics and engineering.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-container" id="index-secondary-content">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>SUBTEAMS</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="content" id="sub-teams">
    <div class="info-blocks" id="mechanical-block">
      <h3>MECHANICAL</h3>
      <div class="blur-load">
        <!-- <img loading="lazy" src={Mechanical.src} alt="gear.png" /> -->
      </div>
      <p>
        From the rigidity of the chassis and suspension to the complexity of the
        arm, the mechanical team is responsible for ensuring the designs meet
        competition specifications and uphold the teams standard of
        functionality by using CAD software, practical experience, and course
        knowledge.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="info-blocks" id="software-block">
      <h3>SOFTWARE</h3>
      <div class="blur-load">
        <!-- <img
              loading="lazy"
              src={Software.src}
              alt=""
              class="bigger-icon-fix"
            /> -->
      </div>
      <p>
        The software team is responsible for designing and developing the
        software that controls the rover. This includes integrating the rover's
        control systems and sensors with the onboard computer, as well as
        creating a graphical user interface on the base station for real-time
        control and sensor data visualization. In the future, the team will
        expand its focus to developing AI that enables the rover to operate
        autonomously and complete tasks without human intervention.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-blocks" id="electrical-block">
      <h3>ELECTRICAL</h3>
      <div class="blur-load">
        <!-- <img loading="lazy" src={Electrical.src} alt="" /> -->
      </div>
      <p>
        Our electrical team carries out many critical jobs within the rover.
        Proper power distribution circuitry for supplying voltage and power
        levels to all circuits within the rover. Moreover, wireless
        communications and sensors used for navigation and control. The
        electrical team carries out these responsibilities to optimize system
        performance in order to carry out operations effectively and reliably.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="info-blocks" id="business-block">
      <h3>BUSINESS</h3>
      <div class="blur-load">
        <!-- <img loading="lazy" src={Business.src} alt="briefcase.png" /> -->
      </div>
      <p>
        The Business Team drives our mission forward by managing finances,
        securing sponsorships, and handling marketing. Just like our rover
        navigates challenges, we strategize to secure resources and maintain a
        strong public presence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
